# Review ownership for the paths that execute.
#
# Everything listed here runs with a credential or ships to users. The release
# workflow fires on a v* tag, configures CMake, compiles the tree and runs every
# tools/test_*.py under `python`, then publishes the result -- so a change to any
# of these paths executes on a runner and lands inside the release zip. Code in
# runtime/, libs/ or include/ has to be compiled into something and deliberately
# run before it does anything; these paths do not.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file does not block a merge. On its own it only *requests*
# review from the owners below -- a PR touching these paths can still be merged
# with that request outstanding. Turning it into a gate takes a branch
# protection rule on `master` with "Require a pull request before merging" plus
# "Require review from Code Owners", which only the repository owner can
# configure. See the PR that added this file.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so order matters: put narrower rules below wider
# ones. A pattern ending in `/` matches the directory and everything under it;
# a leading `/` anchors to the repository root.

# Workflow definitions, their triggers and their permissions. A change here can
# hand a token to anything else in the tree, so it is the widest lever in the
# repository -- including this file.
/.github/              @sp00nznet

# The build system: CMakeLists.txt and the modules it includes both run at
# configure time, before anyone has read the code they are about to compile.
/CMakeLists.txt        @sp00nznet
/cmake/                @sp00nznet

# The Python pipeline. Every tools/test_*.py is executed by the release workflow
# and by each push workflow, and the whole directory is copied into the bundle.
/tools/                @sp00nznet

# Dependency set for those scripts: one added line here is one added package
# installed on a runner and in every contributor's environment.
/requirements.txt      @sp00nznet

# Vendored third-party source, compiled into the shipped runtime library.
/third_party/          @sp00nznet
